{
  "id": "c5",
  "title": "while Loops",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "c5-l1",
      "title": "Repeat with while",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "while (condition) repeats its body as long as the condition is true. The condition is checked before every round, so a loop can also run zero times.",
        "Something inside the loop must change, or the condition stays true forever. An endless loop on a shared PDP-11 would slow down everyone at Bell Labs.",
        "i++ adds 1 to i, i-- takes 1 away. They're the most common lines in any C loop."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    int i = 1;",
          "    while (i <= 5) {",
          "        printf(\"%d\\n\", i);",
          "        i++;",
          "    }",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "1",
          "2",
          "3",
          "4",
          "5"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c5-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When does while check its condition?",
          "options": [
            "Before every round",
            "Only once at the start",
            "After every round",
            "Only at the end"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "If it's false right away, the body never runs."
        },
        {
          "id": "c5-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "#include <stdio.h>",
            "",
            "int main() {",
            "    int i = 3;",
            "    while (i > 0) {",
            "        printf(\"%d\\n\", i);",
            "        i--;",
            "    }",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "options": [
            "3\n2\n1",
            "1\n2\n3",
            "3\n2\n1\n0",
            "nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "i counts down from 3. When it reaches 0, the condition i > 0 is false."
        },
        {
          "id": "c5-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Count up by one.",
          "code": [
            "    while (n < 10) {",
            "        printf(\"%d\\n\", n);",
